# {{label}}

TODO(scaffold): what {{label}} is for a DSP, and the data it shows, in a few lines. Write down any rule that
isn't obvious from the code.

{{#switch}}
- **Switch:** `{{name}}`, off for every DSP until the platform owner switches it on.
{{/switch}}
{{^switch}}
- **Mandatory:** every DSP has it, with no switch to turn it off.
{{/switch}}
{{#permission}}
- **Permissions:** `{{name}}.view`{{#keeps}}, `{{name}}.collect`{{/keeps}}{{#settings}}, `{{name}}.manage`{{/settings}}. Only owners hold them until a role grants them.
{{/permission}}
{{#api}}
- **API:** `GET {{apiPath}}`, behind `{{name}}.view`.
{{/api}}
{{#tables}}
- **Data:** `{{table}}`, in {{databaseLabel}}.
{{/tables}}
{{#keeps}}
- **Keeps:** {{siteLabel}}'s `{{collection}}` collection.
{{/keeps}}
{{#contract}}
- **Exposed:** `{{contract}}`, through its contract in `contract/` (`{{contractCrate}}`), for any feature or agent tool{{#switch}}, while it's on for the DSP{{/switch}}.
{{/contract}}
{{#people}}
- **People:** everyone `{{table}}` names, by their {{peopleSource}} ID, is Driver Match's `{{name}}` kind of data.
{{/people}}
{{#page}}
- **Page:** {{label}}, in a DSP's sidebar.
{{/page}}
{{#tab}}
- **Tab:** {{label}}, on {{hostLabel}}'s page.
{{/tab}}
{{#settings}}
- **Settings:** `{{name}}.general`, "General", on its own page of Settings (`?tab={{slug}}`), behind `{{name}}.manage` (`backend/settings.rs`). Its one field, `example`, is a toggle, off until the DSP turns it on. {{label}} reads it with `backend::settings::general`; core keeps it in the DSP's settings and records each change as `settings.changed`.
{{/settings}}
